  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kondepu Hanumantha Rao vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 16 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5351 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in C.C.No.278 of 2019 on the file of Junior Civil Judge-cum- Judicial Magistrate of First Class, Mangalagiri, Guntur District, which was taken cognizance for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273, 420 of IPC and Section 59(1) of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 01.09.2018 when the complainant along with his staff, on credible information rushed to the house of the accused near Veterinary Hospital of Tadepalli Municipality, searched the house of the accused, found banned tobacco products from his possession, seized the same, arrested the accused and registered a case in Crime No.336 of 2018 of Tadepalli Police Station, for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. He relied upon the order of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018.",
